From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: subarr-subgen <subarr@localhost>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:36:16 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 0065: report which skip rule fired in /batch skip_reasons

/batch returned one `skipped` count, so subarr could not tell "a
target-language subtitle is EMBEDDED in the file" (nothing to do) from
"the audio is a language this subgen skips" (worth a look). Every skip
landed in subarr's Issues bucket as "reason not in /batch response",
including a file carrying three full English tracks (coaxk/subarr#669).

should_skip_file now records its reason in a ContextVar through
_skip_because(<reason>) at every skip branch, from the SKIP_REASONS
vocabulary. Check 4 says whether the target-language copy it found is
embedded (internal_sub) or a sidecar (external_sub); embedded wins when
both exist, since it is the one a user cannot see by listing the folder.
subtitle_exists_in_language passes that along so the container is not
probed twice.

transcribe_existing adds `skip_reasons` ({reason: count}, summing to
`skipped`) to the /batch reply. A skip that recorded no reason counts as
"unknown", and the reason is cleared after every tally so a later file
never inherits an earlier file's rule.

A ContextVar, not a global, so concurrent webhook and /batch calls on
different threads cannot read each other's reason. should_skip_file still
returns a bool, so every other caller is unchanged. The new key is
additive: subarr treats its absence as an older subgen.
---
 subgen.py | 72 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 61 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

